-- title:
--   Completion moments and demand pairings
-- statement:
--   Let $E=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}\times\{0,1\}$, let $B,R\subseteq E$, let $U$ be a set of pair indices, and let $f$ be any real-valued function on subsets of $E$. For a displayed hole $i\in E$, write $\mathcal C(B,R,U;i)$ for the distinct subsets of the form
--   $$
--   B\cup(R\setminus\{i\})\cup\{(t,c(t)):t\in U\},
--   $$
--   where $c$ ranges over Boolean choices. The completion moment and the pairing of a demand node $N=(R,h)$ are
--   $$
--   M_f(B,R,U;i)=\sum_{S\in\mathcal C(B,R,U;i)}f(S),
--   \qquad
--   \langle N,f\rangle_{B,U}=\sum_{i\in R}h(i)M_f(B,R,U;i).
--   $$
--   The sum is over distinct completed states, so different choices producing the same subset are counted only once. No additional weight is inserted into $f$. The coefficient function $h:E\to\mathbb R$ is the demand carried by the node.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/SlotDemandPairing.lean#L18-L24

